    {
      "text": "Table 3: Computational time of different methods on non-continuous tasks.",
      "bbox": [
        155.96400451660156,
        280.97235107421875,
        456.0374450683594,
        289.87890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tasks includes hopper, half-cheetah, ant, walker2d, humanoid-standup, and humanoid-running. The",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        321.8633728027344,
        504.0024108886719,
        330.7699279785156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "selected manipulation task, pushT [15], presents its own challenges due to the complexity introduced",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        332.77337646484375,
        503.9983215332031,
        341.679931640625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "by contact dynamics and the long-horizon nature of the task. These tasks are widely considered",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        343.682373046875,
        503.9974365234375,
        352.58892822265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "difficult due to their hybrid nature and high dimensionality.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        354.59136962890625,
        343.6552429199219,
        363.4979248046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "MBD is compared with the state-of-the-art zeroth-order optimization methods, including CMA-",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        370.9793701171875,
        505.6537170410156,
        379.88592529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ES [7], CEM [11], and MPPI [59], as well as reinforcement learning (RL) algorithms (e.g., PPO [47]",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        381.88836669921875,
        503.99951171875,
        390.794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and SAC [22]) on these tasks. Please note RL is only used for performance reference not as there is",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        392.79736328125,
        504.0032958984375,
        401.70391845703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "no existing TO method that can solve such high-dimensional discontinuous tasks as we have shown in",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        403.7073669433594,
        504.001708984375,
        412.6139221191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the experiments. Model-free RL, especially PPO/SAC, is widely used in such tasks and is considered",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        414.6163635253906,
        504.00152587890625,
        423.5229187011719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the SOTA method. The difference between RL and MBD is further discussed in Appendix A.8 and",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        425.5253601074219,
        504.00421142578125,
        434.4319152832031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "A.6. The RL implementation follows the high-performance parallelized framework from Google",
      "bbox": [
        107.64099884033203,
        436.4343566894531,
        504.0042419433594,
        445.3409118652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Brax [20] elaborated in Appendix A.5.3. For the zeroth-order optimizer, we match the iteration and",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        447.3433532714844,
        504.00396728515625,
        456.2499084472656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sample number with the MBD. All the experiments were conducted on a single NVIDIA RTX 4070",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        458.2523498535156,
        503.9959716796875,
        467.1589050292969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ti GPU. Quantitative metrics including the average step reward and the computational time tested",
      "bbox": [
        107.69100189208984,
        469.1613464355469,
        503.99688720703125,
        478.0679016113281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "over 50 steps repeated for 8 seeds are reported in Tables 2 and 3. MBD substantially outperforms",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        479.3530578613281,
        503.99920654296875,
        489.315673828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "zeroth-order optimization methods and even outperforms RL in most tasks. Specifically, for the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        490.9793701171875,
        503.9974365234375,
        499.88592529296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "pushT task, MBD achieves a significantly higher reward than the RL algorithm thanks to its iterative",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        501.88836669921875,
        504.00250244140625,
        510.794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "refinement process, which effectively explores the full control space while keeping fine-grained",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        512.79736328125,
        503.9974365234375,
        521.7039184570312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "control to precisely push the object. Compared with the computationally heavy RL algorithms, MBD",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        523.7063598632812,
        503.9951171875,
        532.6129150390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "only requires one-tenth of time, which is similar to other zeroth-order optimization methods. The",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        534.6163330078125,
        503.9974060058594,
        543.5228881835938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "optimization process of MBD is visualized in Fig. 3, where the iterative refinement process with the",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        545.525390625,
        503.99609375,
        554.4319458007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "model plays a crucial role in optimizing high-dimensional tasks.",
      "bbox": [
        108.0,
        556.434326171875,
        363.96905517578125,
        565.3408813476562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Figure 4: MBD optimized trajectory with data augmentation on the (a) Humanoid Jogging and (b)",
      "bbox": [
